{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUMQ3WWB7UmjZE9XrhFw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Privately: nothing is left to request. The report section, tables, data, tests, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are all written, the full suite passes, and `solutions/` is untouched. Ten items remain unchecked, so no LOOP_COMPLETE line.\n\n**Item 03 is solved.** The graph story does not hold for the SAT path, and the way it fails is the reduced formula.\n\n**What was built.** `learning/sat_story.py` regenerates §13's re-covering and relabelling pairs from the campaign manifest and runs each through exactly what `decide_mosp` does before the solver, at the refutation and the witness, with a 120 s deadline. Conflicts are counted on CaDiCaL 1.9.5, because the default Kissat backend exposes no statistics through pysat, ignores interrupts, and aborts the interpreter on a conflict budget. Kissat is timed in seconds in a forked, hard-killed child. Ten tests in `tests/test_sat_story.py`, full suite 1,130 passed.\n\n**What was found**, over 3,258 SAT calls at 10 to 30 customers with a small sample at 35:\n\n- Every one of the 5,657 settled decisions on either backend agrees with the certified value.\n- Re-covering the same graph moves the refutation's conflicts. Greedy covers give 0.77 of the base at the median, merges 0.87, splits 1.15, each significant, with a typical pair off by a third. The search's node ratio is 1 on the same pairs.\n- The channel is formula size after dominance. Where a split product is dominated away again, the formula and the conflicts are identical on all 29 such pairs.\n- SAT has a label floor the search lacks. Renaming customers moves refutation conflicts by 1.6 to 1.9 times at the median and witness conflicts by 7 to 13 times.\n- The cover is not why SAT and the search rank instances differently. Within-graph variance is 4 to 21 percent. The rest is between graphs, where SAT tracks clause count and the search does not.\n- The kill test inverts §13. Graph-only features predict SAT conflicts at MAE 0.53 in log10 against 0.25 for the full set.\n\n**Kill verdict.** Met on its letter, failed in its spirit. The pooled median is exactly 1.00 because the methods pull opposite ways and 17 percent of pairs are equal. This is stated plainly in §30 of `reports/ml_nature.md`.\n\n**Caveats recorded.** Refutation censoring at 120 s reaches 62 percent at 30 customers, so paired tables there rest on the easier pairs. Nothing above 35 was run.\n\n**Next item** is 04, the two halves of the `better_move` fix behind flags."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":183908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":736,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0320b61b-4fd3-494e-bf76-e4a32b9df65b","uuid":"7ceff809-ccf5-4d6a-96c1-17f66cf2bcef","timestamp":"2026-09-27T17:39:12.777Z","request_id":"req_011CfUMQ19P4Nz3RdQcVN6b8"}
